From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ashhart <71890694+ashhart@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:03:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/33] prompt cache: each conversation's newest state outlives
 its redundant copies (e5f75e8be, 917a745ad)

Upstream TensorFold commit by ashhart, ported onto this series (see the note below for its upstream source).

Ported by hand from upstream e5f75e8be "Retain each conversation's newest prompt state before redundant
copies" and 917a745ad "cache: distinguish later-turn branches from equal-born reply ends".

A reply end kept with its request's length now links to and supersedes that request's shorter states
unless one is the lookup's selected rewind state (Entry.rewind, Store.active_rewind_key). A resume marks
a state branched only for a real later turn (policy.continuedLater), and an identical re-send adds no
branch. Upstream's test changes come along (branch, warm-pass, index, scan) with its newest-cache tests;
its last test used policy.redundant, which we do not carry, and now checks policy.victim instead.

Added in this series: Store.newest (default true, upstream's order). TENSORFOLD_PCACHE_NEWEST=0 brings back the
old order bit for bit in eviction decisions: equal-born links are still recorded but no longer read.
Replay: --newest 0|1, replay.Config.newest. A new test checks the off order.
